  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A liquid of density $\\rho$ is coming out of a hose pipe of radius a with horizontal speed $v$ and hits a mesh. $50 \\%$ of the liquid passes through the mesh unaffected. $25 \\%$ looses all of its momentum and $25 \\%$ comes back with the same speed. The resultant pressure on the mesh will be:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "YT8uh",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{4} \\rho v^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "YMdE2",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{4} \\rho v^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gFrfV",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2} \\rho v^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "BLdzR",
      "text": "$\\rho v^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Mass per unit time of the liquid = \\rhoav Momentum per second carried by liquid $=\\rho a v \\times v$\r\n\r\nNet force due to bounced back liquid, $\\mathrm{F}_{1}=2 \\times\\left[\\frac{1}{4} \\rho \\mathrm{av}^{2}\\right]$\r\n\r\nNet force due to stopped liquid, $\\mathrm{F}_{2}=\\frac{1}{4}$ pav $^{2}$ Total force,\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{F}=\\mathrm{F}_{1}+\\mathrm{F}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2} \\rho \\mathrm{av}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4} \\mathrm{pav}^{2}=\\frac{3}{4} \\mathrm{pav}^{2}$\r\n\r\nNet pressure $=\\frac{3}{4} \\rho v^{2}$",
    "image": null
  },
